Thanks for comment @reinaldosimoes. As this is just a bug fix to prevent rule from crashing the linter, I won't be making functionality changes. ESLint report is identical with old implementation without optional chaining:

```js
useEffect(() => {}, [someObject?.optionalField.method()]);
useEffect(() => {}, [someObject.method()]);

// Both produce:
// 'React Hook useEffect has a complex expression in the dependency array. Extract it to a separate variable so it can be statically checked.'
// -> No suggestion
```
